Blackdrift: map Focus's colour resources to the Clean Slate tokens.

Why: Focus's palette (Photon violets, the pink accent, purple gradients) is
Firefox Focus's look, and Blackdrift should read as its own product. The 53 light / 51 dark colours
listed in blackdrift/branding/android/focus-colors are rewritten in place in Focus's
own values/colors.xml and values-night/colors.xml, so every resource name
keeps a single definition; a second file defining the same names would break
resource merging. Values are literal hex (main/res cannot see the focus
flavor's blackdrift_* tokens, and klar shares main). Accents become Drift blue,
Erase and error states Thaw red, and the home, header and onboarding
(home_screen_modal_gradient_*) gradients go flat to the ground colour. The
home screen's home_background drawables carry literal gradient stops, so
patch 0209 replaces them, and the Compose palette in ui/theme/FocusTheme.kt
is patch 0210 (hand-written, so this generated patch stays regenerable).
Colours not listed keep their upstream values;
recheck the list when FIREFOX_REV moves (the move to 159.0.1 dropped 18
names that upstream deleted as unused, from 67 to 49, then added the
first-run tip bubble cfr_pop_up_shape_* (light file only) and the white-text
biometric and Add-widget buttons, all Drift blue #2F6FD6). Regenerate with
blackdrift/branding/scripts/apply-focus-colors.mjs.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

